WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.890
Most triumphant!

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.970
We're finally getting a threequel in the saga
of Bill S. Preston, Esquire, and Ted "Theodore"

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:06.970
Logan.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.210
While we can't travel into the future to watch
Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music right now, we've

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.360
rounded up everything we know about their
next (and assuredly, most excellent) adventure.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.360
Keanu Reeves is back

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.980
Before he was Johnny Utah, Johnny Mnemonic,
or John Wick, Keanu Reeves endeared himself

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.010
to audiences as the lovably dimwitted Ted
"Theodore" Logan, who wanted nothing more

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.400
than to make a triumphant music video and
become a famous rock star.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.840
Opposing Ted was his rigid father, whose threats
of sending his son away to military school

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.020
motivated Ted to do whatever it took to pass
his History class and stay at San Dimas high

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.020
school.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.379
Reeves has been talking about a Bill &amp; Ted
sequel for years, although a decade ago, it

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:41.699
barely resembled the movie in its current
form.

00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:45.820
Back in 2008, when Reeves talked to MTV about
a third Bill &amp; Ted, he said it would be a

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.739
remake that wouldn't necessarily involve him,
although he still spoke affectionately about

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:51.739
the possibility.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:54.410
Even back then, though, the seed for Face
the Music seemed to have been germinating

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.449
in Reeves' imagination, with him saying,

00:00:56.449 --> 00:00:59.249
"I had once mentioned about doing it when
we were 40.

00:00:59.249 --> 00:01:02.249
Now maybe the only shot we have is to do it
when we're 50."

00:01:02.249 --> 00:01:07.660
Turns out, he was close; Reeves will be turning
56 just one day after Face the Music arrives.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.650
"But yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.640
Alex Winter is back

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.470
As much as we all love Keanu Reeves, Bill
&amp; Ted doesn't work without a Bill.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.070
Fortunately, Alex Winter is just as stoked
as Reeves to be returning to the role that

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.590
made him famous — as long as it's done right.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.590
Speaking to IndieWire in 2018 about a possible
third film, Winter said,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.190
"We've been pretty philosophical about it,
like if we could get it made, great, but if

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.750
it's not going to get made to our creative
specifications, we're all perfectly happy

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.950
not doing it."

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:38.530
Fortunately, Winter seems to agree with the
consensus that Face the Music is indeed the

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.780
film the original creative team wanted to
make.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.280
It will be Winter's first major starring role
in more than 25 years, after he walked away

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.690
from acting to pursue his passion for documentary
filmmaking, and to give himself space to heal

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:51.450
from the trauma of his childhood.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:56.280
In recent years, Winter has made several documentary
films focusing on technology, including Downloaded

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.500
and Deep Web, and says that making documentaries
is, quote, "the most creatively gratified

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.550
I've ever been."

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.480
Still, Winter was excited to take a short
hiatus from documentaries to step back into

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.440
Bill's high top sneakers and inexplicable
crop top.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.440
Winter added that,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.129
"I really just need to turn that entire side
of my brain off and be the dumbass that Bill

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:14.310
is for three months."

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.310
Death comes for Bill &amp; Ted (again)

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:18.689
Although we're pretty sure that Bill &amp; Ted
Face the Music wouldn't dare kill Bill and

00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:22.439
Ted again, there's still going to be some
role for Death to play in their midlife crisis.

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:26.379
William Sadler is reprising his role as the
Grim Reaper, who failed to permanently collect

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:31.129
the souls of the Wyld Stallyns in Bill &amp; Ted's
Bogus Journey, and subsequently became their

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:32.129
servant.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:34.239
"You have sunk my battleship."

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:39.200
"Excellent!"

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.609
No further details have been revealed about
how Death will figure into Bill &amp; Ted Face

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:47.030
the Music, or whether he'll be functioning
as an ally or an antagonist to the two adorably

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.030
boneheaded heroes.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:52.470
Who knows, maybe he's still a member of Wyld
Stallyns on the upright bass, or has become

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.519
a superstar in his own right following a resurgence
of the popularity of his Reaper Rap.

00:02:56.519 --> 00:02:57.560
Daughters of the Dudes

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:00.879
Just when you thought that Bill &amp; Ted Face
the Music's road to release couldn't get any

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:04.959
more heartwarming, the production had to go
and announce the names of Bill and Ted's daughters.

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:09.370
Ready or Not actress Samara Weaving will be
playing Thea Preston, while Brigette Lundy-Paine

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.989
will be portraying Billie Logan.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:13.810
Yes, Bill and Ted named their daughters after
each other.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.689
This was technically revealed at the end of
Bogus Journey, though many fans simply assumed

00:03:17.689 --> 00:03:20.099
that "Little Bill" and "Little Ted" were boys.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:24.139
As writer Ed Solomon pointed out on Twitter,
though, the kids were played by girls to begin

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:25.139
with.

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:28.390
Producer Scott Kroopf described Weaving and
Lundy-Paine as, quote, "funny and unique,"

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:31.870
to Entertainment Weekly, and said that seeing
them together was like the first time they

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.139
ever saw Winter and Reeves as Bill and Ted.

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:38.200
According to the film's official synopsis,
Billie and Thea will be instrumental in helping

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.150
their dads write the song that will save the
universe.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.150
New princesses

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.819
One of the most excellent parts of Bill and
Ted's first time-hopping adventure was their

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:48.810
stop in medieval England, where they rescued
princesses Joanna and Elizabeth.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.870
Bill and Ted went on to marry the two princesses
off-screen at the end of Bogus Journey during

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.299
their 16 months of intensive guitar training,
and arrived back at Battle of the Bands carrying

00:03:57.299 --> 00:03:59.400
their infant children on their backs.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.010
Now the princesses are back, although they've
been recast for Face the Music.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.389
Jayma Mays of Glee fame will play Bill's wife
Joanna, and Children Hospital's Erinn Hayes

00:04:06.389 --> 00:04:07.480
will play Elizabeth Logan.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.480
New and returning faces

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.750
Were it not for Ted's strict father, Bill
and Ted may never have felt the need to work

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:15.230
so hard to pass history, and embark on their
first voyage through time.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.870
So it's only fitting that the Logan family
will be back for Face the Music, led by Hal

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.340
Landon Jr., who will be reprising his role
as Ted's father.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.960
Meanwhile, Beck Bennett will be taking over
the role of Ted's brother Deacon, replacing

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.300
Frazier Bain, whose career has shifted from
acting to producing.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.620
Hopefully after 30 years, Captain Logan will
have mellowed out a bit when it comes to his

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.410
desire to control his son, but we wouldn't
be surprised if the Captain still somehow

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.570
manages to work the phrase "military school"
into conversation.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:44.510
Meanwhile, Amy Stoch is also returning as
Bill's disturbingly youthful ex-stepmom Missy,

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.250
who married his dad before the start of Bill
&amp; Ted's Excellent Adventure, only to divorce

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.870
him and marry Ted's dad before Bogus Journey.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:54.740
At the end of that film, it's implied that
Missy divorces Captain Logan too, then gets

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:58.740
engaged to the villainous De Nomolos, although
it's never confirmed if she goes through with

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.740
the wedding.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.000
It's unclear what role she'll play in the
adult Bill and Ted's lives in Face the Music,

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.129
but we're sure that however Missy factors
in, it's sure to make Bill uncomfortable.

00:05:07.129 --> 00:05:09.180
"Your stepmom's cute."

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.180
“Shut up, Ted."

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.270
"You know when she was a senior and we were
freshmen?"

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.270
"Shut up, Ted."

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.270
The excellent trailer

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.120
Although Bill &amp; Ted fans have long been champing
at the bit to see our favorite time-traveling

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.400
bozos back in action, we had a long wait to
see any actual footage from Face the Music.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.909
To tide us over while we waited for an official
trailer, Keanu Reeves and Alex Winter, introducing

00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:30.000
themselves in character as "Wyld Stallyns",
filmed a short video at the Hollywood Bowl.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.879
In the video, the pair first announced the
threequel and its title, thanked fans for

00:05:33.879 --> 00:05:37.470
sticking with them, and ended by reminding
us all to be excellent.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:42.500
Finally, in June of 2020, Orion Pictures delivered
the full trailer for Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music,

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.430
and it quickly became clear that the ride
would be worth the wait.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:48.889
The sneak peek offered our first look at our
middle-aged heroes, their kids, and their

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:50.000
old friend Death.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.870
A second trailer followed, promising a return
trip to Hell and setting up the most dire

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.229
stakes of their mission.

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:59.000
It's clear from what we've seen so far that
the classic Wyld Stallyns style of fun is

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.570
alive and well, and we can't wait to see more
in September.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:02.570
A tribute to Rufus

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:06.860
The only major Bill &amp; Ted character not returning
to Face the Music is the duo's time-traveling

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:11.890
mentor Rufus, played by legendary comedian
George Carlin, who passed away in 2008.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.259
Rather than recast Rufus or attempt to sweep
his absence under the rug, Ed Solomon says

00:06:16.259 --> 00:06:19.720
that the third Bill &amp; Ted film will serve
as a tribute to both the character and the

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:20.919
actor who portrayed him.

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:23.849
Solomon said in an interview with Digital
Spy in 2018,

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.629
"George Carlin is so deeply missed by all
of us.

00:06:26.629 --> 00:06:29.610
There is a... not just an homage to him, it's
more than that.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.389
His absence is a part of the whole movie."

00:06:31.389 --> 00:06:34.970
Solomon went on to reveal that Face the Music
will see Bill and Ted interact with their

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.810
younger selves and Rufus by incorporating
footage of Carlin, along with the younger

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.310
Reeves and Winter, from Bill &amp; Ted's Excellent
Adventure.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:45.500
While Rufus may be gone in the upcoming sequel,
he definitely won't be forgotten.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.650
"Be excellent to each other."

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.129
"Party on, dude."

00:06:52.129 --> 00:06:54.620
Some bogus pressure

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.729
Although Bill and Ted actually learned how
to play their instruments and seemingly became

00:06:57.729 --> 00:07:01.740
famous at the end of Bogus Journey, the trailers
for Face the Music tells us that they never

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:04.199
did compose the greatest song ever written.

00:07:04.199 --> 00:07:07.030
Middle age will find them feeling the pressure
of a destiny unfulfilled.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:11.039
According to writers Chris Matheson and Ed
Solomon, the script tackles the pressure of

00:07:11.039 --> 00:07:15.020
being told they're going to save the world
and not having done it yet, and of being 50

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:18.319
and wondering if you should give up on the
dreams you still haven't achieved.

00:07:18.319 --> 00:07:21.430
"You totally blew it, dude."

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.220
The screenwriters went on to explain that
the idea felt much more interesting than telling

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.750
a Bill &amp; Ted story in which they'd already
become famous, saved the world, and had some

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.030
kind of falling out.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.139
Solomon told EW,

00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:34.319
"I think it's kind of like A Christmas Carol
with Bill and Ted.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:37.490
Looking at their lives, and really kind of
rediscovering what they're about."

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.490
A faithful sequel

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.889
The script for Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music has
gone through a lot of changes since Solomon

00:07:41.889 --> 00:07:45.580
and Matheson first pitched the idea to Reeves
and Winter in 2007.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:49.509
However, one thing that's always remained
constant is everyone's desire to make a film

00:07:49.509 --> 00:07:53.229
that feels like it belongs alongside Excellent
Adventure and Bogus Journey.

00:07:53.229 --> 00:07:57.110
No one involved wanted to lose the elements
that make Bill and Ted special, and it sounds

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.500
as though they think they've succeeded.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.500
Reeves told EW,

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:03.430
"I love the characters so much, who they are,
the spirit of their voice that Chris and Ed

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.430
have given [them]."

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.430
Winter added,

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.389
"The whole trajectory of getting the next
one off the ground has been pretty much exactly

00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:10.620
like the experience of getting the original.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.370
Going to every studio, and they're like, 'What
the eff is this?'

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.870
It's this kind of independent spirit, and
the films have an anachronistic quality to

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.560
them that's a big part of what they are, fundamentally.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.310
I'm really happy that this one is the same."

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.310
A tight deadline

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.180
Ever since the official synopsis for Bill
&amp; Ted Face the Music was revealed, we've known

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.509
that the plot would revolve around the two
main characters facing the pressure of not

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:33.229
having yet written their world-saving song
as they stare down the barrel of retirement

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:34.229
age.

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:37.209
However, it now sounds as though the window
in which the duo must deliver their song is

00:08:37.209 --> 00:08:39.780
much narrower than we previously thought.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:44.290
Speaking to EW about Bill and Ted's predicament
in the threequel, writer Chris Matheson revealed,

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.089
"[They've] got literally 80 minutes or all
of reality will come to an end."

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:51.480
With less time to save the world than it would
take to watch either of their previous two

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.880
movies, Bill and Ted will have to make every
second count if they're going to have a chance

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:55.880
of succeeding.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.089
Fortunately, it sounds like they'll have help
from a variety of sources, including their

00:08:59.089 --> 00:09:02.730
daughters, and Kid Cudi's character, who is,
apparently...Kid Cudi?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.529
Director Dean Parisot told EW,

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:05.900
"He plays Kid Cudi.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.130
He gets mysteriously thrown around through
various times, because all time and space

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:10.490
is coming unglued."

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:14.020
Whether Parisot means that Cudi will play
a fictional character similar to his real-life

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:17.960
persona, or an alternate-reality version of
himself, we'll have to wait until the movie

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:20.340
arrives on September 1st to find out.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:23.620
All we can do is hope that it's…

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.620
"Excellent!"

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.860
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:31.490
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:35.050
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

